## Memory Protocol

Persistent memory lives in `.drevon/memory/`, organized as an index plus lazily-loaded detail.

### Reading (cheap)
- **At session start, read only `.drevon/memory/INDEX.md`** — project summary, current focus, one-line
  pointers to every topic file, and the most recent log headlines.
- **Load a topic file only when it is relevant** to the task. Do not read the whole memory directory up front.
- Recall older history with `drevon memory search "<query>"`.

### Writing (via CLI — never hand-edit the log)
| Command | Use when |
|---------|----------|
| `drevon memory log "<what happened>"` | After a significant action |
| `drevon memory decide "<title>" --why "<rationale>"` | A technical decision is made |
| `drevon memory learn "<insight>" --topic <topic>` | A pattern/convention is discovered |
| `drevon memory note "<current focus>"` | The active-work focus changes |

### Topic files
{{#ifEquals mode "hub"}}
| File | Contains |
|------|----------|
| `topics/user.md` | User preferences, feedback, decisions |
| `topics/projects.md` | Registry of workspace projects |
| `topics/systems.md` | Systems & infrastructure |
| `topics/decisions/` | One file per significant decision |
{{else}}
| File | Contains |
|------|----------|
| `topics/architecture.md` | Project context, structure, key files |
| `topics/patterns.md` | Code conventions, gotchas |
| `topics/decisions/` | One file per significant technical decision |
{{/ifEquals}}

### Self-evolution
- Record learnings as you go, but keep it lean — the index is budget-capped.
- If you repeat a multi-step workflow, save it as a reusable prompt in `.drevon/prompts/`.
- Run `drevon memory compact` periodically to keep memory small and fast.
